      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen the model writes text before calling tools, `/v1/responses` returns `[reasoning, message(phase=\"commentary\"), function_call, ...]`. Clients such as Codex replay these items as-is. The `function_call` items carry no `phase`, so `_merge_consecutive_assistant_messages` keeps them apart from the commentary message, and one generated turn is rendered as two assistant messages, the second without reasoning. The history then differs from what the model generated, which also breaks prefix-cache reuse of that turn.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- A tool-call-only assistant message without `phase` merges into a preceding `commentary` message.\n\n## Tests\n\nReplaying `[reasoning, message(commentary), function_call x2, function_call_output x2]` now yields one assistant message with `reasoning_content`, `content` and both `tool_calls`. `test/registered/unit/entrypoints/openai/test_serving_responses.py` results are unchanged versus main.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41869837316](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41869837316)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41869836967](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41869836967)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41869837296](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41869837296)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -